Transcript:\n- Good afternoon and\na warm welcome to you, our in-house 
audience,\nand to the many viewers who are watching us on Zoom. My name is 
Claire Lyons\nand I'm the curator of antiquities here at\nthe Villa and the 
curator of the new exhibition now\non view on the second floor, “The Kingdom of 
Pylos:\nWarrior-Princes of Mycenaean Greece.” Today is a celebration for us. The
villa reopened to the public yesterday and this is our...\n(audience applauds) 
Yeah. This is our first in-person program after the Palisades fire 
swept\nthrough six months ago. Local friends and neighbors will find the 
surrounding area much\nchanged from the absence of over 1,400 trees that\nwere 
cut on this property. But fortunately, our building and collection were 
safeguarded,\nand it's truly wonderful to see visitors here once again. 
Recognizing the Gabrieleño\nTongva people whom we honor as the original 
caretakers\nof this place known as Tovaangar, planning is already underway to 
reimagine the site's\nnative environment, its landscapes, and vistas. This 
afternoon's lectures\ncelebrate the reopened villa as well as a landmark 
