wording may vary slightly; the sentence is reconstructed from a snippet.", 
"paraphrase"]}, {"id": "20260628151100437036_d2463ad0", "type": "Document", 
"source_id": "20260628151100138803_64a1bc49", "text": "The 2014 University of 
Birmingham PhD thesis \"An analysis of Late Bronze Age Aegean glyptic motifs\" 
surveys motifs found on Late Bronze Age Aegean seals and signet rings. Within 
its discussion of dating and the interpretive limits of iconographic evidence, 
the thesis references scholarship on the Ring of Nestor, including an article 
published in the Oxford Journal of Archaeology (OJA 17(1), 1–13, 2002) devoted 
to the ring. The thesis notes that certain scenes do not contain iconographic 
information that allows precise dating, placing the Ring of Nestor within a 
broader debate about how far glyptic imagery can be used to establish 
chronology. The work uses the ring as part of its wider corpus of examples 
rather than as the primary focus, and it situates the ring’s imagery among 
broader categories of motifs in Aegean glyptic."}, {"id": 
"20260628151101394178_541c015f", "type": "Statement", "confidence": "medium", 
"qualifiers": [], "source_id": "20260628151100082676_286f4fca", "text": "The 
same article argues that table altars depicted on Minoan gold rings, including 
those interpreted on the Ring of Nestor, likely represent wooden, portable 
altars that were used for sacrifices.", "statement_key": 
"statement:eda3d0d41086beff683fd26b", "document_id": 
"20260628151100364287_80337f22", "limitations": ["The argument is summarized 
from a brief mention in the snippet; the supporting archaeological evidence and 
full context are not reproduced."]}, {"id": "20260628151100138803_64a1bc49", 
