    "raw_content_or_summary": "This Perspectives article from the Metropolitan 
Museum of Art discusses historic photographs and reproductions of Aegean Bronze 
Age artifacts and the role of Émile Gilliéron (father and son) in creating 
casts, watercolors, and other reproductions. Among the objects mentioned in 
passing are the \"Ring of Nestor\" and the Phaistos Disk. The article notes that
the Harvard Art Museums hold a collection of fifteen Gilliéron reproductions, 
and that such replicas were widely circulated among institutions in the early 
20th century. The Met's article is focused on the history of documentation and 
reproduction rather than on the detailed provenance or current location of the 
original Ring of Nestor, but it situates the ring within a network of museums 
that collected reproductions tied to Evans' work at Knossos and other Aegean 
sites."
