      "document_summary": "Rhiannon E. Palmer’s 2014 University of Birmingham 
PhD thesis analyzes Late Bronze Age Aegean glyptic motifs of a religious nature 
and includes discussion of the Ring of Minos and the Ring of Nestor in the 
context of authenticity debates. In one passage Palmer notes that the Ring of 
Minos (identified as AM 1938.1110) and the Ring of Nestor (identified as VI.277)
have both been denounced as fakes by Nilsson (1950) and Biesantz, among others. 
The thesis explicitly treats AM 1938.1110 as an Ashmolean Museum inventory 
number, but presents VI.277 without explanation of whether it is a museum 
accession or a corpus/catalogue reference. Throughout the thesis, corpus 
references such as the Corpus der minoischen und mykenischen Siegel (CMS) are 
used, but the specific passage mentioning VI.277 does not define this identifier
or link it to a museum, accession number, or current location of the Ring of 
Nestor.",
