and includes the Ring of Nestor among its examples. In the text, the Ring of 
Nestor is explicitly referred to as CMS VI 277 and is described as said to be 
from a tholos tomb in Kakovatos. The article uses the CMS designation (Corpus 
der minoischen und mykenischen Siegel) as the primary identifier for the ring 
and emphasizes its traditional provenance rather than providing a museum 
accession number or clear information on its current institutional holding.",
      "source_ref": "s2"
