craftsmanship: Vlachopoulos discusses the ring as a gold signet ring, addresses 
manufacturing techniques, stylistic traits, and compares its workmanship with 
securely provenanced Minoan and Mycenaean glyptic.", "Corpus identification: the
Ring of Nestor is catalogued as entry no. 277 in volume 6 of the Corpus der 
minoischen und mykenischen Siegel, confirming its inclusion in the standard 
glyptic corpus.", "Existence of detailed iconographic description focused on 
