{"query": {"id": "20260628150925031584_b74967c1", "handle": "q1", "text": "“Ring
of Nestor” Mycenaean gold ring archaeological object discovery context", 
"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628151254706054_43e93dc4", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "论文对“Ring of 
Nestor”的图像进行细致分解，将戒面上的人物、祭坛、树木和动物等要素与已知米诺斯、
迈锡尼金戒图像进行一一对比，以评估其是否符合青铜时代爱琴艺术传统。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628151254759750_f19ff552", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Hudler 记载“Ring 
of Nestor”被描述为在靠近皮洛斯的 Kakovatos 
一座石室墓中出土，并将这一出土地信息与其作为“dubitanda”的学术地位联系起来。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151252971610_85a3f3b7"], "citations": [16]}, {"id": 
"20260628151254822660_6a5655da", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Hudler 
的案例研究追踪“Ring of 
Nestor”的研究史，列出多位学者对其真伪发表的观点，并讨论这些观点在网络和数字平台
上的再传播。", "source_ids": ["20260628151252971610_85a3f3b7"], "citations": 
[16]}, {"id": "20260628151254891262_0b0ae0a2", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"剑桥章节指出，“Ring of 
Nestor”图像中可以辨认出乘船的女性人物、祭坛、圣树和贝提勒等要素，这种复杂组合在
爱琴青铜时代金戒中较为罕见，因此长期成为学界关注焦点。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151252992632_80181a53"], "citations": [17]}, {"id": 
"20260628151254953343_61da765a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "该章节将“Ring of 
Nestor”纳入“Fakes and 
Dubitanda”一章，以其出土地记载不清、风格混合以及与已知伪造者活动时间相吻合等因素
为例，说明识别青铜时代爱琴伪作的困难。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151252992632_80181a53"], "citations": [17]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255016896_371eea96", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Marinatos 
在大都会博物馆的文章中写道，她认为“Ring of Minos”和“Ring of Nestor”都是由 Émile 
Gilliéron fils 伪造的戒指，并给出了风格与档案证据以支持这一判断。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151253014064_8bb784f2"], "citations": [18]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255080094_594510b9", "type": "Evidence", "text": "文章列举 Gilliéron
fils 制作与修复其他青铜时代文物的实例，指出“Ring of 
Nestor”的图像构图与他已知的重构手法高度相似，从而加强伪作假说。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151253014064_8bb784f2"], "citations": [18]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255134481_dbdfda3c", "type": "Evidence", "text": "《Traces of 
Places》一文在讨论某枚金戒时提到，“在所谓‘Ring of 
Nestor’上，这一构件被解释为狮鹫的座位”，用以说明戒面上为神话生物预留的座位如何在
图像中标示神圣空间。", "source_ids": ["20260628151100082676_286f4fca"], 
"citations": [6]}, {"id": "20260628151255191715_b3bb159b", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "该文将“Ring of 
Nestor”的祭坛、树木和座位等图像元素与其他米诺斯金戒进行并列分析，认为这些微缩景
象共同构成对特定圣地的视觉再现。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100082676_286f4fca"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255247712_ee65ccf9", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"研究雅典卫城金戒的论文指出，“Ring of 
Nestor”被登记为阿什莫尔博物馆藏品，并在讨论中利用该戒指展示博物馆档案如何记录来
自 Kakovatos 石室墓的金戒。", "source_ids": ["20260628151253053625_bd320d09"], 
"citations": [19]}, {"id": "20260628151255303040_7fd57edf", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "论文比较雅典卫城金戒与“Ring of 
Nestor”的所谓出土地叙述，指出两者都存在由收藏者或中间商提供、而非由正式考古报告
记录的出土地信息。", "source_ids": ["20260628151253053625_bd320d09"], 
"citations": [19]}, {"id": "20260628151255356868_3d56b67e", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "科学期刊中的金制品技术研究在参考文献中引用了“The ring of Nestor. A 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world. London …”，说明“Ring of 
Nestor”作为讨论米诺斯来世观或宗教理念的案例被频繁引用。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151253079840_1a40ec4c"], "citations": [20]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255416475_5d389f24", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"该技术研究通过对四座石室墓中金戒的微量元素与制作工艺分析，建立这些墓葬金制品的
年代与工艺序列，为将“Ring of 
Nestor”与有明确出土背景的金戒进行技术比较提供了潜在参照。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151253079840_1a40ec4c"], "citations": [20]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255471090_38502d04", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Davis 与 Stocker 
描述，在“狮鹫武士”墓中发现的四枚金印章戒饰有米诺斯仪式场景，这些戒指与墓葬其他高
等级随葬品一起被置于晚赫拉迪克 IIA，构成该墓主人身份与文化联系的重要证据。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151253100552_dd1e4d6e"], "citations": [21]}, {"id": 
"20260628151255526499_9e720260", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"文章指出，这些带有神祇、祭坛与神圣树木图像的金戒显示出强烈的米诺斯风格，说明迈
锡尼精英在宗教图像上采纳并改造了克里特传统。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151253100552_dd1e4d6e"], "citations": [21]}, {"id": 
"20260628151455477189_75ead60f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
generally treated in scholarship as a Mycenaean-type gold signet ring whose 
bezel depicts a complex ritual or sacred scene including human figures, an 
altar, tree(s), animal(s), and other cultic elements such as a seat interpreted 
as a griffin’s throne and sacred stones (baetyls).", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f", "20260628151100082676_286f4fca", 
"20260628151252992632_80181a53"], "citations": [2, 6, 17]}, {"id": 
"20260628151455720011_7dcb272b", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
widely cited in scholarship on Minoan–Mycenaean gold rings, religion, and sacred
landscapes, and has become a key comparative case for discussing Minoan ritual 
imagery and conceptions of the afterlife or sacred places.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100082676_286f4fca", "20260628151252971610_85a3f3b7", 
"20260628151253079840_1a40ec4c", "20260628151253100552_dd1e4d6e"], "citations": 
[6, 16, 20, 21]}, {"id": "20260628151455872614_6011505d", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The Ring of Nestor is commonly described as having come from a chamber 
tomb at Kakovatos near Pylos, with a discovery date around the turn of the 19th 
to 20th century, but the documentary record for its findspot, circumstances of 
discovery, and early collecting history is incomplete and problematic.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151252971610_85a3f3b7", "20260628151252992632_80181a53",
"20260628151253053625_bd320d09"], "citations": [16, 17, 19]}, {"id": 
"20260628151456030319_d6a8df91", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
reported as being registered in the collection of the Ashmolean Museum in 
Oxford, where archival records associate it with gold rings said to come from 
the Kakovatos chamber tombs near Pylos.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151253053625_bd320d09"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628151456122540_2dad4e13", "type": "Claim", "text": "The authenticity of 
the Ring of Nestor is strongly contested: it is listed among Aegean Bronze Age 
‘fakes and dubitanda’, and Nanno Marinatos argues, on stylistic, technical, and 
archival grounds, that the Ring of Nestor (like the Ring of Minos) was 
fabricated in the early 20th century by Émile Gilliéron fils rather than being a
Bronze Age original.", "source_ids": ["20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f", 
"20260628151252971610_85a3f3b7", "20260628151252992632_80181a53", 
"20260628151253014064_8bb784f2"], "citations": [2, 16, 17, 18]}], "offset": 0, 
"limit": 20, "total": 21, "next_offset": 20}
[tools:c596d94a-dc66-868c-3a3e-ef75a0ba4d45] [get_report_evidence result] 
{"query": {"id": "20260628150925126858_787b2bc9", "handle": "q2", "text": "“Ring
of Nestor” detailed description dimensions material iconography scene analysis",
"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628151101825175_ec291f8c", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "“The Ring of Nestor, measuring 3.29 cm by 2.18 cm, is the 
fifth largest Aegean signet ring.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059895146_c51fb205"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151101896562_fbe3ecab", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The chapter 
associates the Ring of Nestor with Aegean gold signet rings and situates its 
craftsmanship within established categories of Minoan and Mycenaean glyptic 
work, in the context of a discussion on authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059895146_c51fb205"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151101971155_8c26422a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The author 
contrasts earlier claims that the Ring of Nestor might be a forgery with more 
recent research that, in his view, confirms the ring’s authenticity.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151059895146_c51fb205"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102037195_eaa53bd7", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The chapter 
appears in a volume on Aegean iconography and includes a detailed description 
and interpretation of the ring’s scene, addressing the figures, spatial setting,
and possible ritual or religious context.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059895146_c51fb205"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102111830_e83efa0f", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The paper is 
described as presenting an analysis of the iconography surrounding the “Ring of 
Nestor” in the context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102180138_f4c16ddc", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Within its 
analysis, the paper discusses the figural composition on the ring’s bezel, 
including the number and type of figures, associated symbols such as altars, 
trees, animals, or celestial signs, and the arrangement of these elements into a
narrative or ritual scene.", "source_ids": ["20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628151102252883_eb6bf976", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The volume’s reference list includes: “Evans, ‘“The Ring of Nestor”: a 
glimpse into the Minoan afterworld and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet 
rings from Thisbe, Boeotia’, JHS 45, 1–75.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059991695_781fe51a"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102322818_812beeba", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Evans title as
cited in the Aegis volume characterizes the Ring of Nestor as providing “a 
glimpse into the Minoan afterworld” and as part of “a sepulchral treasure of 
gold signet rings from Thisbe, Boeotia.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059991695_781fe51a"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102399526_c0d3fe79", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The AJA review 
states that in the Corpus der minoischen und mykenischen Siegel the Ring of 
Nestor appears as no. 277.", "source_ids": ["20260628151100022629_e8d266c5"], 
"citations": [4]}, {"id": "20260628151102464725_20584065", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The review observes that while some may still harbor doubts as to the 
authenticity of the “Ring of Nestor” (no. 277), other suspect pieces in the 
corpus have been reassessed differently.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100022629_e8d266c5"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102540592_2f1a9f36", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Cain notes that 
drawings of impressions of gold rings with epiphany scenes, including the Ring 
of Nestor (cited via Evans PM III, 145–57), are used in his comparative 
analysis.", "source_ids": ["20260628151100055197_4068b239"], "citations": [5]}, 
{"id": "20260628151102608776_1daa1efc", "type": "Evidence", "text": "A figure 
caption in Cain’s article is summarized in the snippet as “Fig. 9. Drawing of 
impression of gold ring with epiphany scene …”, with the Ring of Nestor included
among the rings discussed.", "source_ids": ["20260628151100055197_4068b239"], 
"citations": [5]}, {"id": "20260628151102673844_4353f063", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The snippet from “Traces of Places” indicates that on the Ring of 
Nestor a griffin is described as using a structural element on the ring as a 
seat: “Ring of Nestor serves as a seat for a grif[f]in.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100082676_286f4fca"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102741041_f330f2d1", "type": "Evidence", "text": "In the same 
context, the article explains that table altars were probably wooden and 
portable, and when used for sacrifices they were situated in specific contexts, 
drawing on imagery that includes rings such as the Ring of Nestor.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151100082676_286f4fca"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151102809132_b95edca8", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Dartmouth 
Aegean Prehistoric Archaeology bibliography lists: “Evans, ‘The “Ring of 
Nestor”: A Glimpse into the Minoan After-world,’ JHS 45 …” among its references 
for the lesson.", "source_ids": ["20260628151100109801_853bf17c"], "citations": 
[7]}, {"id": "20260628151102878552_6b836884", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
Birmingham thesis’ bibliography includes the reference: “Ring of Nestor'', OJA 
17 (1), 1–13. 2002.”", "source_ids": ["20260628151100138803_64a1bc49"], 
"citations": [8]}, {"id": "20260628151102946672_f6b16c1f", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "In a discussion of dating, the thesis remarks that “None of the scenes 
contain any iconographic information that points to a date …”, in a context that
includes reference to scholarship on the Ring of Nestor.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100138803_64a1bc49"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260628151525981140_8a91b691", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
a Late Bronze Age Aegean gold signet ring measuring approximately 3.29 cm by 
2.18 cm, and its craftsmanship has been analyzed in relation to established 
Minoan and Mycenaean glyptic work.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151059895146_c51fb205"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151526069870_fd8670e6", "type": "Claim", "text": "Within the standard 
Aegean seal corpus, the Ring of Nestor is catalogued as entry no. 277 in volume 
6 of the Corpus der minoischen und mykenischen Siegel.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151100022629_e8d266c5"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151526127194_ee784ff2", "type": "Claim", "text": "Scholarly opinion on 
the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor has been divided, but recent research, 
including Vlachopoulos’ analysis of its manufacture and style, argues that the 
ring is authentic.", "source_ids": ["20260628151059895146_c51fb205", 
"20260628151059963850_4b6ddc5f", "20260628151100022629_e8d266c5"], "citations": 
[1, 2, 4]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 20, "total": 26, "next_offset": 20}
