[8]}, {"id": "20260628151421181393_54381b9b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
Biblioteka Nauki article quotes or paraphrases Evans’ description of the Ring of
Nestor as offering \"a glimpse into the Minoan after‑world\" and forming part of
a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead seals from Thisbê, 
Boeotia.", "source_ids": ["20260628151417761251_2daa045d"], "citations": [22]}, 
{"id": "20260628151421246247_27cc4b3f", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
Biblioteka Nauki article states that the Ring of Nestor is dated to the Late 
Bronze Age and may have been manufactured in a Minoan workshop before being 
