["20260628151417782383_dd950f89"], "citations": [23]}, {"id": 
"20260628151421470641_be1e9a4f", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The sphag- article
affirms that the Ring of Nestor belongs to the Late Bronze Age Mycenaean 
iconographic corpus and is relevant for understanding representations of 
slaughter, blood, and sacrifice.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151417782383_dd950f89"], "citations": [23]}, {"id": 
"20260628151421526144_86a3e0c4", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The sphag- article
notes that scholars disagree over whether scenes on rings like the Ring of 
Nestor depict actual ritual practices or abstract ideological imagery.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151417782383_dd950f89"], "citations": [23]}, {"id": 
"20260628151421583479_ed1f4749", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The composite 
