contain unresolved disagreement on the following point: Vlachopoulos 2020 
presents the suspicion that the Ring of Nestor is a forgery as a past scholarly 
tendency that has now been completely reassessed in favor of authenticity, 
whereas the JAEI article’s title and wording foreground the concept of a 
\"Pseudo-Minoan\" Nestor Ring and states that many scholars condemned it as a 
forgery, implying ongoing or renewed skepticism. [51][1]\n\nPublic sources still
contain unresolved disagreement on the following point: The convergence of 
Vlachopoulos’s claim that the ring’s authenticity has been documented and 
reassessed completely in its favor with the ResearchGate article’s statement 
that new technical observations support authenticity contrasts with the 
continued framing of the ring as problematic in the JAEI article and with 
reported remarks in the AJA review that some scholars still harbor doubts. 
